    <innerclass refid="classthemis_1_1timeseries_1_1_ts_edge_case_handler" prot="public">themis::timeseries::TsEdgeCaseHandler</innerclass>
    <innernamespace refid="namespacethemis">themis</innernamespace>
    <innernamespace refid="namespacethemis_1_1timeseries">themis::timeseries</innernamespace>
    <briefdescription>
<para>Deterministic edge-case handler for remote-write and encrypted chunk scenarios in the ThemisDB timeseries module. </para>
    </briefdescription>
    <detaileddescription>
<para>Provides TsEdgeCaseHandler, which enforces deterministic fail-safe behavior across:</para>
<para><itemizedlist>
<listitem><para>Remote-write validation errors (invalid endpoint, auth failure, timeout)</para>
</listitem><listitem><para>Encrypted chunk edge cases (null key, rotation during write, truncated chunk)</para>
</listitem><listitem><para>Buffer pressure edge cases (full out-of-order buffer, forced re-sort trigger)</para>
</listitem><listitem><para>Retention policy boundary conditions (exact boundary eviction, concurrent expiry)</para>
</listitem></itemizedlist>
</para>
<sect1 id="ts__edge__case__handler_8h_1autotoc_md29_1s1"><sect2 id="ts__edge__case__handler_8h_1autotoc_md29">
<title>Result Convention</title><para>All operations return <computeroutput>std::optional&lt;TimeseriesErrorCode&gt;</computeroutput>:<itemizedlist>
<listitem><para><computeroutput>std::nullopt</computeroutput> — success</para>
</listitem><listitem><para>non-nullopt — the specific error code describing the failure</para>
</listitem></itemizedlist>
</para>
</sect2></sect1>
<sect1 id="ts__edge__case__handler_8h_1autotoc_md30_1s1"><sect2 id="ts__edge__case__handler_8h_1autotoc_md30">
<title>Design Principles</title><para><orderedlist>
<listitem><para><bold>Fail-Safe</bold>: all error paths return structured error codes rather than propagating exceptions to callers.</para>
</listitem><listitem><para><bold>Bounded Behavior</bold>: all operations complete within documented time bounds or emit a TIMEOUT incident.</para>
</listitem><listitem><para><bold>Isolation</bold>: encryption key lifecycle events do not interrupt in-flight ingest or query operations.</para>
</listitem><listitem><para><bold>Thread-Safety</bold>: all public methods are safe for concurrent invocation.</para>
</listitem></orderedlist>
</para>
<para><simplesect kind="see"><para><ref refid="timeseries__api__contract_8h" kindref="compound">include/timeseries/timeseries_api_contract.h</ref> — base error taxonomy </para>
</simplesect>
<simplesect kind="see"><para>src/timeseries/ROADMAP.md — Phase 2/3 Q4 2026 items </para>
</simplesect>
</para>
</sect2></sect1>
